- op: discuss  # a5db
  at: '2026-09-28T06:27:14Z'  # a5db
  by: agent  # a5db
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a5db
  clock: 4  # a5db
  nonce: a5db  # a5db
  message: "Fixed in PR #1266 (5c72e23fa2). _extract_use_aliases now reads the declaration's namespace_name prefix and the clauses inside namespace_use_group, and accepts a bare name (or qualified tail) as the clause path inside a group -- both halves of the root_cause. Behavioural evidence on merged dev, the item's own repro: alias map 'use Foo\\{Bar, Baz};' -> {Bar: Foo\\Bar, Baz: Foo\\Baz} (was {}), 'use Foo\\{Bar as B};' -> {B: Foo\\Bar} (was {}), single-import control unchanged; hypergumbo survey (cold cache): the grouped-import call helper() -> php:Foo\\helper:0-0:helper (was php:external:0-0:helper), identical to the single-import form. Also covered: use function / use const groups, mixed-kind groups, multi-segment prefixes (test_php_grouped_use.py). 'use Foo;' still registers nothing, as before. Corpus effect: none measurable locally (0 grouped of 5,323 namespace imports, 09-27 count), so not claimed as recall."  # a5db
